---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Check the selected source through the correctness and compiler observation owners

Usage: pse check [OPTIONS] [PACKAGE[:TARGET]]...

Arguments:
  [PACKAGE[:TARGET]]...  Workspace package names, optionally followed by :TARGET. Use -p for opaque package IDs

Options:
  -C <checkout>
  -p, --package <SPEC>             Package to process (see `cargo help pkgid`)
      --format <FORMAT>            Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --workspace                  Process all packages in the workspace
      --fields <FIELDS>            Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --budget <BUDGET>            Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact
      --exclude <SPEC>             Exclude packages from being processed
      --all-features               Activate all available features
      --no-default-features        Do not activate the `default` feature
  -F, --features <FEATURES>        Space-separated list of features to activate
      --without-feature <ABSENT>   Features that the actual selected compiler roots must keep absent
      --target <PLATFORM>          Explicit Cargo target platform; host dependency contexts remain independent
      --target-kind <TARGET_KIND>  Disambiguate duplicate target names by their Cargo kind, for example test or bin
      --detach                     Return the original managed launch identity and leave its owner running
      --session <SESSION>          Correlate this operation with an agent session without granting control authority
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Check the selected source through the correctness and compiler observation owners

Usage: pse check [OPTIONS] [PACKAGE[:TARGET]]...

Arguments:
  [PACKAGE[:TARGET]]...
          Workspace package names, optionally followed by :TARGET. Use -p for opaque package IDs

Options:
  -C <checkout>


  -p, --package <SPEC>
          Package to process (see `cargo help pkgid`)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --workspace
          Process all packages in the workspace

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact

      --exclude <SPEC>
          Exclude packages from being processed

      --all-features
          Activate all available features

      --no-default-features
          Do not activate the `default` feature

  -F, --features <FEATURES>
          Space-separated list of features to activate

      --without-feature <ABSENT>
          Features that the actual selected compiler roots must keep absent

      --target <PLATFORM>
          Explicit Cargo target platform; host dependency contexts remain independent

      --target-kind <TARGET_KIND>
          Disambiguate duplicate target names by their Cargo kind, for example test or bin

      --detach
          Return the original managed launch identity and leave its owner running

      --session <SESSION>
          Correlate this operation with an agent session without granting control authority

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
